# L §7.1: date literals ("months, quarters or years used as dates or keys") appear only in rows, governs, asks ...;
# "A rule can't test m >= 2028-01 on a time key" (LOAD-LITERAL). A quarter in a def's comparison is refused.
# (Writer 8: the built-in index quarters is gone, L §2.2, §4.1 "A quarter ... is a value, never a key"; the
# comparison now reads quarter_of of an input's date.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input d0: date

def early: bool = quarter_of(d0) <= 2026-Q2
ask a: early
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LITERAL a date in a rule; make it a version (m.tally:11)
